    {
      "text": "if he ask a fish, will he give him a serpent, Matt. 7:10 (Luke 11:11; 3 Ne. 14:10). wise as serpents, and harmless as doves, Matt. 10:16 (D&C 111:11). Ye serpents, ye generation of vipers, Matt. 23:33. They shall take up serpents; … not hurt them, Mark 16:18 (Morm. 9:24; D&C 84:72; 124:99). unto you power to tread on serpents, Luke 10:19. as Moses lifted up the serpent … so must the Son of man, John 3:14. as the serpent beguiled Eve … so your minds should be corrupted, 2 Cor. 11:3. great dragon was cast out, that old serpent … the Devil, Rev. 12:9. he laid hold on … that old serpent … and bound him a thousand years, Rev. 20:2.",
